; link/pop_cels.link — the scene's CEL IMAGE, its own link unit at $C000 (P3.69/P3.71).
;
; WHAT THIS IS. The cutscene's cel pixels and the [cel][facing][phase] table that indexes
; them, linked at $C000 and read off disk into a GIME bank that cutscene_room.s maps
; there through $FFA6/$FFA7. It contains NO code and is never executed — it is an asset
; that happens to be assembled, because the table's entries are label references the
; linker has to resolve against the cel data sitting beside it.
;
; WHY IT LEFT THE FLAME BUNDLE. The bundle had reached 11,921 B against the 14,848 B
; between FLAME_BASE ($3000) and the disk driver's parameter block at $6A00, with five
; scene beats still to add (P3.62 measured the remaining ones as not fitting in either
; representation). The cels are the majority of that and the part that never executes,
; so they are the part that can live behind a window register. The bundle drops to
; ~4,280 B and the beats have room again.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; $C000 IS NOT ARBITRARY, AND IT IS NOT THE FRAMEBUFFER.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The draw window is $8000-$FFFF, four MMU registers $FFA4-$FFA7 (gfx.s GFX_DB_WINDOW /
; GFX_DB_MMU / GFX_DB_BLOCKS). The scene runs 4-colour, so its framebuffer is 15,360 B
; and occupies only $8000..$BBFF — the window's lower half. $C000-$FFFF is the RESERVED
; TAIL of a 32 KB-per-buffer allocation that 4-colour never uses, which is precisely why
; a bank can be mapped there without touching a pixel. In 16-colour it could not: a
; 30,720 B framebuffer needs all four blocks, which is the same fact HAL_gfx_mirror's
; guard checks before it borrows $C000 for the front buffer.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE `load` VALUE IS BARE HEX, AND $C000 WOULD SILENTLY LINK AT ZERO.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; `section prog load $C000` parses the `$` form as 0 — no error, no warning, exit 0, and
; the image lands at $0000. This is the SAME trap build.bat documents one tool along for
; `lwasm -D` (a $-prefixed value defines as zero, which put the disk parameter block
; inside the HAL's DP scratch band). Two different tools, one shape of silence.
;
; It is caught rather than trusted: decb_to_raw.py refuses an image whose first segment
; is not exactly at the `--base` build.bat states, so a drift between this line and
; build.bat is a build error instead of a black scene.
;
; Comments in this file are `;`. lwlink does NOT accept `*` here — that is an assembler
; convention, and using it is a parse error, not a comment.

section prog load C000

entry cel_image
